body: "The `release` job of the Daily Release workflow failed.\n\n- Failing job: `release`\n- Run URL: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-csv/actions/runs/40177055905\n- Commit: 07bc618897f18d396395a71c5034cf5f30aff5af\n- Date (UTC): 2026-10-25T09:32:34Z\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-25T23:08:43Z)\n>\n> Recovered: the 2026-10-25 run failed only at \"Merge release metadata through protected PR\". The release PR's required checks were still queued when the 30-minute merge wait expired, because the runner pool was saturated; no check failed. The run was re-run (or, where main had advanced, dispatched fresh), and v2026.10.25 is published: npm `pm-csv@2026.10.25` and GitHub Release v2026.10.25 (2026-10-25T10:31:49Z). Future runs that fail this way are recovered automatically by the host-side release re-run sweep (unbraind/pm-cli-companion#273)."
